"><path d=\"M9 7a3 3 0 0 1 3-3h5a3 3 0 0 1 3 3v5a3 3 0 0 1-3 3h-1v-2h1a1 1 0 0 0 1-1V7a1 1 0 0 0-1-1h-5a1 1 0 0 0-1 1v1H9V7zm-5 5a3 3 0 0 1 3-3h5a3 3 0 0 1 3 3v5a3 3 0 0 1-3 3H7a3 3 0 0 1-3-3v-5zm3-1a1 1 0 0 0-1 1v5a1 1 0 0 0 1 1h5a1 1 0 0 0 1-1v-5a1 1 0 0 0-1-1H7z\"/></svg>\n            <span>Copy link</span>\n          </button>\n        </nav>\n      \n    </header>\n    <aside class=\"ad-placement ad-placement--blog_story_root ad-placement--adsense\" aria-label=\"Advertisement\"><span class=\"ad-placement__label\">Advertisement</span><div class=\"ad-placement__body\"><ins class=\"adsbygoogle\" style=\"display:block\" data-kt-ad-pending=\"true\" data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-3019430404409047\" data-ad-slot=\"3403651247\" data-ad-format=\"auto\"  data-full-width-responsive=\"true\"></ins></div></aside>\n\n    \n      \n      \n      \n        <figure class=\"article-image\">\n          <img data-story-image referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://cdn.uzalendonews.co.ke/original/2026/10/1001558591.webp\" sizes=\"(max-width: 860px) 100vw, 820px\" alt=\"Spain’s Ferran Torres Withdraws from Nations League Camp with Ankle Injury\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" loading=\"eager\" fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\">\n          \n        </figure>\n      \n    \n\n    <div class=\"article-body\">\n      <aside aria-label=\"Advertisement\" class=\"ad-placement ad-placement--article_before_first_paragraph ad-placement--adsense\"><span class=\"ad-placement__label\">Advertisement</span><div class=\"ad-placement__body\"><ins class=\"adsbygoogle\" data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-3019430404409047\" data-ad-format=\"horizontal\" data-ad-slot=\"4593428073\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\" data-kt-ad-pending=\"true\" style=\"display:block\"></ins></div></aside><p>Paris Saint‑Germain forward Ferran Torres was released from the Spanish national team camp after the Spanish Football Federation confirmed he had been suffering left‑ankle pain for several days.</p>\n<p>The 26‑year‑old will miss Spain’s next UEFA Nations League fixtures against the Czech Republic and Croatia, as the federation prioritised his recovery and gave no timetable for his return.</p>\n<p>Real Madrid’s 21‑year‑old forward Carlos Espi has been called up to replace Torres in the squad for the two matches.</p><aside aria-label=\"Advertisement\" class=\"ad-placement ad-placement--article_after_paragraph_3 ad-placement--adsense\"><span class=\"ad-placement__label\">Advertisement</span><div class=\"ad-placement__body\"><ins class=\"adsbygoogle\" data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-3019430404409047\" data-ad-format=\"auto\" data-ad-slot=\"4593428073\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\" data-kt-ad-pending=\"true\" style=\"display:block\"></ins></div></aside>\n<p>Torres’ departure follows recent exits by winger Nico Williams and left‑back Alejandro Grimaldo, marking the third Spanish player to leave the camp early in recent days.</p>\n<p>Spain entered the Nations League campaign strongly, opening Group A3 with a 3‑2 win over England at Wembley and following it with a 4‑1 victory against Croatia in Seville.</p>\n<p>Torres had featured prominently in the earlier part of the international window before the ankle issue forced his withdrawal.</p>\n<p>The injury also concerns PSG, which will monitor Torres’ condition closely as the club awaits his return from international duty.</p>\n    </div>\n    <aside class=\"ad-placement ad-placement--article_after_body ad-placement--adsense\" aria-label=\"Advertisement\"><span class=\"ad-placement__label\">Advertisement</span><div class=\"ad-placement__body\"><ins class=\"adsbygoogle\" style=\"display:block\" data-kt-ad-pending=\"true\" data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-3019430404409047\" data-ad-slot=\"4593428073\" data-ad-format=\"auto\"  data-full-width-responsive=\"true\"></ins></div></aside>\n\n    \n  </article>\n\n  \n    <section class=\"content-band related-band\">\n      <div class=\"section-head\">\n        <h2>Related stories</h2>\n      </div>\n      <div c